WEBVTT

00:06.506 --> 00:09.300
[sweet airy music]

00:42.542 --> 00:43.668
All right, where do I begin?

00:43.752 --> 00:45.086
[inhales]

00:45.170 --> 00:47.505
First, let me tell you
a little bit about myself.

00:47.589 --> 00:49.883
[crew] Pick up the pace,
we're out of time. Hurry!

00:51.217 --> 00:53.511
- [Chi-seong] Here.
- What's next?

00:53.595 --> 00:56.431
[NJ] You can say I've always lived
a very professional life.

00:56.514 --> 00:58.558
- Pose for us.
- NJ over here!

00:58.641 --> 01:00.185
- [shutters clicking]
- [photographers calling]

01:00.268 --> 01:02.062
- NJ, I need a shot of you!
- Smile!

01:02.562 --> 01:03.688
That's right, pose for us.

01:03.772 --> 01:05.231
[NJ] My life is glamorous

01:06.316 --> 01:08.234
with a lot of passion and devotion.

01:10.153 --> 01:11.738
All right, now forget about that.

01:12.447 --> 01:13.615
Wanna know the real me?

01:20.538 --> 01:21.706
EYE MAGIC
SHINE LIKE MAGIC

01:30.173 --> 01:33.009
Then we gotta talk about
someone else in my story.

01:36.930 --> 01:40.141
Here's a guy popping out of nowhere
like it was fate.

01:40.225 --> 01:41.643
[deep yawn]

01:41.726 --> 01:43.937
Okay, maybe not so much.

01:46.356 --> 01:48.483
[cheerful music]

01:49.484 --> 01:50.401
HAVER
NJ

01:51.611 --> 01:52.987
NJ PURCHASES A FIVE-STORY BUILDING

01:53.071 --> 01:55.907
Amazing. News travels really fast.

01:55.990 --> 01:59.035
- [trol 1] She bought another building?
- [trol 2] Never enough for that princess.

01:59.119 --> 02:02.080
Another article about you?
Whatever it is, just ignore it for now.

02:02.163 --> 02:04.874
Easier said than done,
you don't know what they wrote about me.

02:05.458 --> 02:08.253
So many ads nowadays,
you can barely see anything.

02:08.837 --> 02:09.796
Shit.

02:10.380 --> 02:11.923
Oh, come on.

02:12.590 --> 02:16.219
[NJ] I guess it could've been big data
scientifically matching us up.

02:16.928 --> 02:18.054
They look kinda…

02:18.138 --> 02:20.765
GO-OH

02:21.474 --> 02:23.017
…strangely weird.

02:23.101 --> 02:23.935
GO-OH'S SOLO EXHIBITION

02:24.018 --> 02:26.896
As it happened,
right after purchasing a building,

02:26.980 --> 02:30.400
I ended up going to an exhibit
of someone who only drew buildings.

02:32.152 --> 02:34.112
And that's where him and I met each other.

02:36.322 --> 02:40.076
I know it's crinkled and messy,
but it's clean.

02:41.369 --> 02:42.829
What's this for?

02:42.912 --> 02:44.414
Well, you're crying and…

02:48.168 --> 02:49.043
[door opens]

02:51.754 --> 02:54.048
Oh, sorry, the layout is
a little confusing, but

02:54.132 --> 02:56.009
you can start over there,
it's a lot easier.

02:56.092 --> 02:57.844
[visitor] Oh, is that so? Thank you.

03:04.434 --> 03:06.019
[both chuckle]

03:06.102 --> 03:07.729
- Thank you for that.
- [chuckles]

03:09.480 --> 03:10.815
I guess I look silly?

03:12.233 --> 03:15.028
[NJ] Crying while staring blankly
at a drawing of a building.

03:15.820 --> 03:17.739
Mm… Sounds pretty normal.

03:18.448 --> 03:20.909
You ever cry over a drawing of a building?

03:20.992 --> 03:22.118
Uh…

03:23.244 --> 03:24.495
Exactly.

03:25.622 --> 03:27.498
Not really something a normal person does.

03:30.126 --> 03:31.085
Hmm…

03:32.795 --> 03:35.882
But still, feel free to come here
and cry whenever you want.

03:37.300 --> 03:40.136
If you want, I'll cry with you
so it's not too weird.

03:43.223 --> 03:44.474
[chuckling]

03:45.683 --> 03:48.102
One of the worst
pick-up lines I've ever heard.

03:48.186 --> 03:49.771
I was trying to make you feel better.

03:49.854 --> 03:52.774
You make it a habit, comforting strangers?

03:52.857 --> 03:57.111
Uh, it doesn't feel like you're
a stranger, I see you a lot on TV.

03:57.195 --> 03:58.738
So it kinda feels like I already know you.

03:58.821 --> 04:00.156
I'm a big fan of yours.

04:00.240 --> 04:01.366
[chuckles softly]

04:01.449 --> 04:03.284
Bro! I need you to…

04:03.368 --> 04:05.578
[light music]

04:08.289 --> 04:09.290
Yo…

04:10.500 --> 04:12.877
[Eun-ho] Hey, bro, where are you?
You over here?

04:12.961 --> 04:14.337
Yo!

04:14.420 --> 04:17.215
[NJ] Something smelled kinda fishy,
so I had to get to the bottom of it.

04:17.298 --> 04:19.092
Are you part of the staff here?

04:19.175 --> 04:21.344
Oh, no. I'm just a visitor.

04:21.427 --> 04:23.304
Are you familiar with the artist?

04:23.388 --> 04:25.014
Oh, no. Just a visitor.

04:25.098 --> 04:27.392
I'm interested in buying this.
How much you want for it?

04:27.475 --> 04:28.601
It's ten million…

04:31.020 --> 04:33.106
I don't wanna guess, I'm just a visitor.

04:33.189 --> 04:34.691
You can go there and ask,
maybe they'd know.

04:34.774 --> 04:37.318
Guess is not just the drawings
that are strange.

04:37.402 --> 04:38.945
- Huh?
- What?

04:39.028 --> 04:41.698
Oh, nothing.
So where do I ask about buying it again?

04:41.781 --> 04:45.285
[Eun-ho] I don't want you putting a single
scratch on it. Please be careful with it.

04:45.368 --> 04:48.496
GO-OH'S SOLO EXHIBITION

04:48.579 --> 04:51.666
[NJ] Like I said,
I was gonna get to the bottom of it.

04:51.749 --> 04:53.209
May I ask for your phone, please?

04:53.293 --> 04:55.378
- [NJ] I am a busy woman, but still…
- What?

04:55.461 --> 04:57.255
So if I ever get bored
of that drawing of yours,

04:57.338 --> 04:58.673
I can just buy another.

04:58.756 --> 05:00.008
Yeah, but I said it wasn't me.

05:00.091 --> 05:01.092
Oh, really?

05:01.592 --> 05:04.012
- I think I should get a refund then.
- Uh.

05:07.140 --> 05:09.225
- Please don't tell anyone.
- [chuckles]

05:09.309 --> 05:12.061
[NJ] This, now this was fun.

05:13.062 --> 05:14.731
[phone buzzing]

05:14.814 --> 05:18.318
This is my number.
Not a lot of people have it.

05:18.401 --> 05:21.654
Not a lot of people have my number either.
I don't have much friends.

05:21.738 --> 05:23.448
[awkward chuckle]

05:23.531 --> 05:25.908
[NJ] Now, I wanna make myself
perfectly clear…

05:25.992 --> 05:28.786
Anyway, I'll just give you a call later.

05:28.870 --> 05:31.205
ARTIST GO-OH

05:31.289 --> 05:33.833
[NJ] …this isn't something
that I would normally do…

05:33.916 --> 05:35.251
- Sure.
- [NJ] …that much.

05:35.335 --> 05:37.086
[Mi-yeon] Wonder how long
this one will last.

05:37.170 --> 05:39.297
There's absolutely
no information about him.

05:39.380 --> 05:41.299
Did they ever finish
that diagnosis on your brain?

05:41.382 --> 05:42.216
Yes.

05:42.925 --> 05:44.886
Hmm, I'm just a romantic.

05:44.969 --> 05:46.721
Hmm, I think you mean lunatic.

05:46.804 --> 05:49.307
You're interested for one or two months
and then act all cold after.

05:49.390 --> 05:52.435
[NJ] Every individual is unique,
and we all have our own ways.

05:53.061 --> 05:56.064
There you have it,
that's basically how our story began,

05:56.647 --> 05:59.984
turns out, he was more interesting
than I initially thought.

06:00.068 --> 06:01.694
And I mean a whole lot more.

06:02.862 --> 06:05.114
[uplifting music]

06:06.741 --> 06:09.118
This caused a bit of a problem for me.

06:12.038 --> 06:13.915
Mr. Choi, what you doing?

06:13.998 --> 06:15.917
- [message pings]
- [Ung] Prepping some beansprouts.

06:16.000 --> 06:18.044
[NJ] God, it's really
scorching out there today.

06:18.127 --> 06:19.128
What you doing right now?

06:19.212 --> 06:21.923
[Ung] Doing some weeding.
Feels like my hair is on fire.

06:22.006 --> 06:23.841
[NJ] Gave a really good performance today.

06:23.925 --> 06:26.052
Why aren't you watching?
What are you so busy doing?

06:26.135 --> 06:29.514
[Ung] I'm eating right now.
I can just pay the 1500 and rewatch it.

06:30.056 --> 06:31.349
[chuckles softly]

06:33.726 --> 06:37.647
[NJ] Mr. Choi, I know it's late,
but I hope you can answer this question.

06:38.689 --> 06:39.816
What you doing right now?

06:39.899 --> 06:43.152
I seriously thought that he would just
pop into my head every now and then.

06:43.236 --> 06:44.821
Who? That person again?

06:48.157 --> 06:49.617
[delighted chuckle]

06:52.245 --> 06:53.287
Choi Ung!

06:53.371 --> 06:55.248
[NJ] So I wanna find out for myself

06:55.873 --> 06:57.792
is this just another one of those

06:57.875 --> 06:59.877
- short-lived feelings fleeting?
- Oh!

06:59.961 --> 07:01.879
- [chuckles]
- [NJ] Or will this one be different?

07:02.505 --> 07:03.631
[NJ] And you know what?

07:04.257 --> 07:06.425
I don't think it'll take long to find out.

07:06.509 --> 07:13.516
EPISODE 10
HELLO, MY SOUL MATE

07:21.149 --> 07:22.358
What are you two doing?

07:24.902 --> 07:27.321
[awkward music]

07:30.491 --> 07:31.826
Uh…

07:31.909 --> 07:35.204
Know what this is?
It's our first day anniversary!

07:35.288 --> 07:36.956
[chuckles awkwardly]

07:37.039 --> 07:40.168
I mean as friends, as friends.
Wow, a day already?

07:40.710 --> 07:41.627
Time flies.

07:43.129 --> 07:45.256
So are you doing a documentary or a skit?

07:47.758 --> 07:49.552
Well, what are you
even doing here at this hour?

07:49.635 --> 07:51.053
You didn't text or call.

07:51.137 --> 07:52.430
Actually, you didn't pick up.

07:52.513 --> 07:53.681
[inhales]

07:53.764 --> 07:56.809
Seeing you together late at night
looking like this…

07:56.893 --> 07:58.436
seems strange is you ask me.

07:58.519 --> 08:00.646
Um, I know. I get that
this looks a little weird,

08:00.730 --> 08:02.440
- and you could probably take this--
- Not at all.

08:02.523 --> 08:05.568
You probably got tired of arguing
and decided to bury the hatchet.

08:05.651 --> 08:07.778
- Exactly. What you said. Exactly.
- Hmm.

08:07.862 --> 08:10.615
[Yeon-su chuckles awkwardly]

08:11.157 --> 08:13.117
[awkward music continues]

08:24.545 --> 08:26.589
- I'm sleeping over.
- What?

08:27.215 --> 08:28.966
Hey. My house look
like a motel or something?

08:29.050 --> 08:31.469
Why has everyone
been bunking up here lately?

08:31.552 --> 08:32.887
Why? Who else slept here?

08:34.055 --> 08:37.183
Uh… Eun-ho. You know that punk.

08:37.266 --> 08:38.184
Shit.

08:40.353 --> 08:41.312
[sighs]

08:42.563 --> 08:43.648
[awkwardly clears throat]

08:44.524 --> 08:46.567
Are you guys gonna just stand there?

08:46.651 --> 08:50.071
Oh, it's getting late,
so I should get going now.

08:50.154 --> 08:51.739
[Ung] Wait. What about the chicken?

08:51.822 --> 08:54.450
- What? Sad to see me go?
- In your dreams.

08:54.534 --> 08:56.035
Besides, late-night snacks are unhealthy.

08:56.118 --> 08:57.620
Says the one who ordered it.

08:57.703 --> 08:59.580
All right, I'm off now. You two have fun.

08:59.664 --> 09:01.749
Yeon-su, just call a cab. It's dark.

09:01.832 --> 09:03.000
It's okay. I'll just walk.

09:03.084 --> 09:05.711
- I ordered some chicken--
- Hey. Just go.

09:10.675 --> 09:12.552
Okay, okay, no need to push me.

09:12.635 --> 09:16.597
If you go now you can still catch the bus.
Take number four. Don't walk home.

09:19.183 --> 09:20.643
[scoffs]

09:22.562 --> 09:24.480
[beeping]

09:26.774 --> 09:29.026
[gentle music]

09:41.664 --> 09:42.915
What?

09:45.126 --> 09:46.085
[Ji-ung] Nothing.

09:48.713 --> 09:50.047
[groaning sigh]

09:51.215 --> 09:53.426
[sighs]
Finally, a little peace.

09:55.386 --> 09:57.847
It'd be great
if a certain someone also left.

09:57.930 --> 09:59.849
No need to get your panties in a bunch.

10:00.433 --> 10:02.059
- You eat yet?
- Hmm, I did.

10:02.768 --> 10:04.729
Ooh. Chicken will be here soon.

10:06.314 --> 10:07.148
[puffs]

10:07.231 --> 10:09.108
Did you order some beer with that?

10:11.485 --> 10:12.445
Mm-hmm.

10:14.864 --> 10:16.782
[creaking]

10:18.075 --> 10:19.452
[creaking continues]

10:36.427 --> 10:37.637
- [switch thuds]
- [gasps]

10:38.638 --> 10:39.972
[sigh of relief]

10:40.056 --> 10:41.349
Oh, God, you startled me.

10:41.432 --> 10:43.601
I almost got a heart attack, grandma!

10:43.684 --> 10:46.604
You little brat.
Do you know what time it is?

10:46.687 --> 10:49.607
So what? I always come home late.
I come home around this time--

10:49.690 --> 10:52.026
You're late by about 24 hours.

10:52.109 --> 10:54.654
I told you I'd be sleeping over
at my friend's house.

10:54.737 --> 10:56.656
I'm not a kid anymore. Take it easy.

10:56.739 --> 10:59.575
I always do this, don't tell me
this is why you're still up this late.

10:59.659 --> 11:01.452
Nice try.
You don't have any friends, you liar.

11:01.535 --> 11:04.872
What? Well, you don't have to hurt
your granddaughter's feelings like that.

11:04.955 --> 11:06.499
Where'd you stay over? Huh?

11:07.416 --> 11:10.002
I slept at Sol-i's.
You know I always do that.

11:10.086 --> 11:12.880
Hey, Yeon-su. Long time no see.
How's everything?

11:14.340 --> 11:16.050
When did you get… Why are you here?

11:16.133 --> 11:18.511
You little wench. How dare you lie to me?

11:18.594 --> 11:21.222
Tell me the truth.
Where did you sleep, you hussy?

11:21.305 --> 11:23.933
Leave it to me, grandma,
I'll interrogate the suspect.

11:24.016 --> 11:26.310
It's getting late. Go to bed. Go on.

11:26.394 --> 11:28.687
She's seeing some guy,
you can bet on that.

11:28.771 --> 11:30.564
- Okay, but that's good news.
- Of course it is.

11:30.648 --> 11:33.692
- Then why'd you slap her?
- Because I'm curious about whoever it is.

11:33.776 --> 11:35.277
Find out. I wanna know about it.

11:35.361 --> 11:37.822
You know I can hear you guys, right?

11:37.905 --> 11:40.533
[chuckles]
Can you really? Let's go in.

11:42.034 --> 11:44.578
[Sol-i] You have the right
to remain silent, young lady.

11:49.875 --> 11:51.168
What are you doing in my house?

11:51.252 --> 11:53.295
I bumped into your grandma in the alley.

11:53.879 --> 11:56.799
Funnily enough, she thought
you were sleeping over at my place.

11:56.882 --> 12:00.261
Should have told me about it before
so I could have backed up your lies.

12:00.344 --> 12:01.720
I didn't lie to anyone.

12:03.013 --> 12:05.057
How dare you say that to me.

12:05.141 --> 12:07.059
- What kind of friend do you think I--
- Choi Ung.

12:07.143 --> 12:08.727
I slept over at Ung's place.

12:08.811 --> 12:10.438
Yeah, I figured that.

12:10.521 --> 12:12.982
He said he wants to try
being friends for a change.

12:13.566 --> 12:14.650
What?

12:14.733 --> 12:17.611
That's right. He wants us to be friends.

12:17.695 --> 12:19.113
[scoffs]

12:19.196 --> 12:21.699
Nice to see you two still being boneheads.

12:22.950 --> 12:25.536
It's weird.
This is all a bit weird, right?

12:25.619 --> 12:27.913
Hey. Friend or not,
he doesn't deserve you.

12:27.997 --> 12:29.290
What's his deal anyway?

12:33.043 --> 12:35.212
And then? What did you say?

12:35.296 --> 12:36.839
Did you say okay?

12:38.132 --> 12:39.884
- Just for now.
- Ooh.

12:39.967 --> 12:41.427
Just for now?

12:41.510 --> 12:42.761
[gasps]

12:42.845 --> 12:45.181
Then what? What's your plan?

12:46.182 --> 12:50.728
That plan is, I'm gonna figure out
how he really feels while being friends.

12:51.645 --> 12:53.272
I'm going to make him admit to it.

12:53.856 --> 12:56.442
What kind of a confession exactly.

12:57.860 --> 13:02.114
Yeon-su, this isn't a crime movie.
It's romance.

13:02.198 --> 13:04.283
He's not some perp you're trying to catch.

13:04.366 --> 13:06.577
He's basically you're secret crush.

13:07.369 --> 13:08.287
My…

13:09.914 --> 13:13.334
No! I don't have a crush on him.
Don't be dumb. There's no secret.

13:13.417 --> 13:15.085
[gasps]
So what's all this then?

13:16.170 --> 13:18.923
I just… I just wanna know
what's on his mind

13:19.006 --> 13:20.633
so no one gets the wrong idea.

13:21.217 --> 13:23.636
You're curious
about his innermost thoughts

13:23.719 --> 13:25.679
because you want him to feel the same way.

13:26.263 --> 13:29.600
Don't hide it, darling. That's what
having a secret crush feels like.

13:29.683 --> 13:30.684
[groans]

13:31.602 --> 13:33.312
Go to bed. Stop thinking about him.

13:33.395 --> 13:35.898
I never said I was thinking about him.
Don't be ridiculous.

13:35.981 --> 13:37.024
[Sol-i] Secret crushes.

13:37.107 --> 13:38.692
I've had a few myself.

13:39.276 --> 13:40.986
If you have any questions, ask away!

13:41.070 --> 13:42.738
I don't have a crush on him!

13:43.364 --> 13:44.198
[gasps]

13:44.281 --> 13:47.368
Interesting, so you're saying that
it's a lot more serious than I thought?

13:47.451 --> 13:48.869
- Looks like the flame never went out.
- It's not like that.

13:48.953 --> 13:50.955
- Shut your stupid mouth!
- [groans]

13:51.038 --> 13:53.290
- Wow, that'll set you on fire.
- [groans]

13:54.667 --> 13:56.669
You can barely contain yourself
when I mention him--

13:56.752 --> 13:58.087
[Yeon-su] I said, that's not true!

14:02.883 --> 14:04.260
[rustling]

14:08.639 --> 14:11.058
[exclaims]
Hurry up and get over here!

14:14.436 --> 14:15.646
- [Ji-ung] It's here?
- Yep.

14:15.729 --> 14:16.647
[groans]

14:17.565 --> 14:18.691
[Ung groans]

14:19.525 --> 14:20.818
[both groan]

14:24.572 --> 14:27.074
[soft calm music]

14:28.784 --> 14:29.702
Mm…

14:30.786 --> 14:32.746
[crunching]

14:45.301 --> 14:47.177
[Ung] So how many shoots do we have left?

14:48.053 --> 14:50.014
Just three. Wrapping up next week.

14:50.973 --> 14:54.184
How's the whole thing going?
Not exactly like you planned?

14:54.268 --> 14:56.770
Well, since you're aware of that,
maybe you'd like to take

14:56.854 --> 14:58.564
a little bit more initiative
on things, huh?

14:58.647 --> 15:00.107
Maybe you can stop running away.

15:00.190 --> 15:01.191
[Ung] Hmm.

15:04.862 --> 15:05.863
[Ji-ung sighs]

15:07.364 --> 15:09.325
[music fades]

15:10.576 --> 15:11.660
[Ung inhales]

15:11.744 --> 15:14.163
So what's with that look
you've been giving me lately, huh?

15:14.997 --> 15:16.749
Yo. Tell me what's on your mind.

15:16.832 --> 15:19.960
Don't worry, if it's all bullshit anyway,
I'll filter it out myself.

15:21.378 --> 15:23.547
I have been meaning to ask you something.

15:25.215 --> 15:26.342
But never mind.

15:26.926 --> 15:28.052
Whatever, dude.

15:28.135 --> 15:29.303
I get to think however I want.

15:30.721 --> 15:32.389
[scoffs]
Son of a bitch.

15:32.473 --> 15:35.100
I appreciate the creative way
of being annoying you've achieved.

15:41.357 --> 15:42.358
[soft sigh]

15:42.441 --> 15:45.736
What? Is there something
going on with you?

15:47.613 --> 15:49.031
[Ung] I mean you're…

15:49.114 --> 15:52.451
You're not a drinker,
and suddenly, you wanna drink. Also…

15:53.535 --> 15:55.204
You haven't slept here in ages, dude.

15:56.080 --> 15:59.667
I just… I don't feel like going home.

16:04.421 --> 16:05.422
Why?

16:06.048 --> 16:08.092
You get nervous
whenever big bro sleeps over?

16:08.175 --> 16:11.303
[scoffs]
Are you drunk? Wash up and go to bed.

16:11.387 --> 16:12.972
And by the way,

16:13.514 --> 16:16.141
it has been ages
since we've had some alone time, huh?

16:16.684 --> 16:18.602
Ungie, wanna sleep together?

16:18.686 --> 16:20.270
[chuckles, inhales]

16:20.354 --> 16:24.066
Oh, God. If you ever wondered, this is why
I don't like drinking with lightweights.

16:24.149 --> 16:25.401
Sleeping already?

16:25.484 --> 16:27.903
[Ung] Nah, I'm going to work a bit
before that. Go to sleep.

16:27.987 --> 16:29.989
Who the hell works after drinking?

16:30.614 --> 16:32.825
- [Ung] Jesus. Shut up.
- Hey, no, don't go yet!

16:33.575 --> 16:34.910
I'm not sleepy.

16:36.829 --> 16:37.997
Here.

16:38.080 --> 16:39.039
[groans]

16:39.123 --> 16:41.041
While I'm still being nice,
just go to sleep.

16:41.125 --> 16:43.419
Or else I'm gonna kick you out.
Good night.

16:46.171 --> 16:48.090
[sighs, groans]

16:50.968 --> 16:51.885
[soft groan]

16:56.932 --> 16:58.600
[soft music]

16:58.684 --> 17:00.811
[groans]

17:11.780 --> 17:13.907
[soft music continues]

17:29.131 --> 17:31.258
[music fades]

17:32.342 --> 17:33.469
[sighs]

17:34.762 --> 17:36.930
[cameraman] The camera is ready to go.
Are you good?

17:37.973 --> 17:39.183
[Ji-ung] You're here early.

17:41.477 --> 17:43.103
- [Ji-ung] How's the background?
- [cameraman] Good. Okay.

17:43.187 --> 17:46.523
Oh, and you can sit right there.
We'll start whenever you're ready.

17:51.111 --> 17:53.072
[quirky music]

17:54.948 --> 17:56.992
You left it there on purpose.

17:57.076 --> 18:00.204
No, I didn't.
I really did forget all about it.

18:00.287 --> 18:01.497
[scoffs]

18:01.580 --> 18:04.958
So your legit excuse for going back there
is that you left a pouch behind.

18:05.042 --> 18:07.252
Huh. Couldn't think
of anything better than that?

18:07.336 --> 18:09.171
I'm not making excuses, it's true.

18:09.254 --> 18:11.090
That pouch has always been
like a treasure to me.

18:11.173 --> 18:14.343
Fine. Makes perfect sense.
So let me get this straight,

18:14.426 --> 18:16.220
I literally begged you
to have lunch with me.

18:16.303 --> 18:19.348
But then, all of a sudden,
you gotta go back to you-know-who

18:19.431 --> 18:21.308
'cause you left your pouch over there.
[gasps]

18:21.391 --> 18:23.936
I wonder why.
Oh, can I guess, pretty please?

18:25.104 --> 18:26.688
Girl, you're as transparent as ever.

18:26.772 --> 18:28.857
That's the most obvious excuse
so you can go back there

18:28.941 --> 18:30.984
and have a lovely lunch date
with just the two of you.

18:31.068 --> 18:32.486
What? That's nuts.

18:32.569 --> 18:34.321
Yeah? Tell me I'm wrong.

18:35.197 --> 18:37.074
[gasps]
Wow. I'm impressed.

18:37.157 --> 18:38.367
How in the world did Ung manage

18:38.450 --> 18:40.452
to wrap you around
his little finger like this?

18:40.536 --> 18:42.371
For real, I'm genuinely curious.

18:42.454 --> 18:43.497
[gasps]

18:43.580 --> 18:46.959
Oh, my God, everyone! This girl has fallen
head over heels for her crush.

18:47.042 --> 18:49.336
She's so caught up by her feelings
that's she's even left me

18:49.419 --> 18:50.587
to starve to death all by myself!

18:50.671 --> 18:53.590
Can you stop saying
that I have a crush on him?

18:53.674 --> 18:54.883
Have a nice day.

18:56.885 --> 18:58.637
I'm gonna have a blissful meal all alone.

18:58.720 --> 19:00.514
That's right, all by myself.

19:01.140 --> 19:02.391
Go be happy, Yeon-su.

19:03.183 --> 19:04.560
Good luck, Yeon-su.

19:05.269 --> 19:06.311
[chuckles]

19:12.151 --> 19:14.278
[cheeky music]

19:28.208 --> 19:30.460
Hello, everyone.
I'm Choi Ung's friend, NJ…

19:32.045 --> 19:34.756
Can I use a fake name?
Because I didn't get permission yet.

19:34.840 --> 19:38.969
Can you blur out my face?
No, wait. I'll look like a criminal then.

19:40.179 --> 19:41.597
All right, let's roll.

19:42.306 --> 19:44.016
- Oh.
- [thuds]

19:48.312 --> 19:50.272
[NJ] So what do you wanna know today?

19:50.355 --> 19:52.065
You want me to talk about Choi Ung?

19:55.986 --> 19:56.904
[Sol-i] Mmm.

20:01.241 --> 20:03.118
- I remember now!
- Holy! what the…

20:03.827 --> 20:05.746
- Wow.
- What are you doing here?

20:05.829 --> 20:07.080
You went to that bar over there

20:07.164 --> 20:08.707
so you can steal the recipes
from their menu, remember?

20:08.790 --> 20:10.334
- Huh?
- Wow.

20:10.417 --> 20:13.003
What are you doing here? Do you work here?

20:13.086 --> 20:15.547
Yeah, sometimes. I help out
during the days that they're busy.

20:15.631 --> 20:18.550
Oh, I knew you looked familiar.
Something about you was bugging me.

20:19.259 --> 20:21.595
Tell me, are you doing
market research again?

20:21.678 --> 20:23.138
- I don't do that.
- [chuckles]

20:24.181 --> 20:25.515
Are you close with the owner or something?

20:25.599 --> 20:27.726
Huh? Didn't you know?

20:27.809 --> 20:29.186
- What?
- Look at the name.

20:30.354 --> 20:32.981
- It says "With Ung."
- Hmm. So what?

20:35.067 --> 20:36.860
[gasps dramatically]
No way.

20:36.944 --> 20:40.364
Huh. How could you miss that?
Your shop's literally nearby.

20:40.447 --> 20:42.741
Ji-ung's parents run this restaurant?

20:42.824 --> 20:44.618
- [Sol-i] Wow. Crazy.
- [chopsticks clink]

20:44.701 --> 20:46.245
His family is wealthy.

20:46.328 --> 20:47.621
No wonder.

20:47.704 --> 20:51.333
You ever consider that maybe it's
Choi Ung's parents who own this place?

20:51.416 --> 20:53.794
Right. Come on.
Ji-ung's the one who actually looks more--

20:53.877 --> 20:55.629
It's owned by Choi Ung's parents.

20:55.712 --> 20:57.673
In fact, they own
all the restaurants in this area.

20:57.756 --> 20:59.258
- [gasps softly]
- [chuckles]

20:59.341 --> 21:02.552
But you're correct, Ung doesn't exactly
look like he's from a wealthy family.

21:02.636 --> 21:04.972
But yeah, he was born
with a silver spoon in his mouth.

21:05.055 --> 21:06.515
I just got goosebumps.

21:08.308 --> 21:11.561
Looks like he finally has
one charming trait under his sleeve.

21:11.645 --> 21:14.314
Not bad, Yeon-su,
guess you are a cunning girl.

21:14.898 --> 21:17.818
- Why? What about Yeon-su?
- Hmm? Nothing.

21:17.901 --> 21:19.444
Are you sure that's all that you need?

21:19.528 --> 21:22.364
- [NJ] I have much more I can tell you.
- [Ji-ung] No, this is more than enough.

21:22.447 --> 21:24.574
That's weird. I didn't know
they were filming today.

21:25.659 --> 21:27.953
Same here. I'm as surprised
as you are right now.

21:29.496 --> 21:30.998
What are you doing back here?

21:31.581 --> 21:34.584
Oh, I just left something at your place.

21:34.668 --> 21:36.044
- Mr. Choi.
- [Yeon-su gasps]

21:36.712 --> 21:38.297
Were you watching the whole time here?

21:38.380 --> 21:41.675
You shouldn't have.
It was supposed to be a surprise for you.

21:41.758 --> 21:43.760
That doesn't make sense.
Why would you do it at my place?

21:43.844 --> 21:47.723
Why? For convenience sake, of course.
We're gonna go on a date today.

21:47.806 --> 21:50.642
[gasps, chuckles awkwardly]
I wouldn't call it that.

21:50.726 --> 21:53.520
Are you Kook Yeon-su?
We've actually met, if you don't remember.

21:54.104 --> 21:54.980
Right.

21:55.063 --> 21:57.065
I enjoyed your documentary.

21:58.191 --> 22:01.028
- Mr. Kim, is it okay if I go?
- Sure.

22:01.111 --> 22:03.280
I'm famished.
You haven't eaten yet, have you?

22:03.363 --> 22:04.823
- Let's go and take care of that.
- Oh…

22:04.906 --> 22:07.034
Hey, wait. Ung!

22:07.117 --> 22:09.411
I… I left something at your place.

22:09.494 --> 22:11.830
I need to go and get it right now
if that's okay.

22:12.331 --> 22:13.832
Right now? What is it?

22:13.915 --> 22:16.376
It's something I need.
It's super precious to me.

22:16.460 --> 22:18.378
Fine, just look for it yourself.

22:18.462 --> 22:20.130
But that wouldn't be right,
it's your house.

22:20.213 --> 22:22.674
Um, so what? You're used to it.

22:22.758 --> 22:24.176
Uh, but still…

22:24.968 --> 22:26.303
I'll see you next time.

22:27.262 --> 22:29.014
[NJ] Shall we? Where to?

22:31.099 --> 22:32.267
[NJ chuckling]

22:33.101 --> 22:34.519
[Ji-ung] You good to film?

22:35.687 --> 22:37.522
What? Film what?

22:38.774 --> 22:40.650
- Thank you very much. Bye.
- Thank you as well.

22:42.069 --> 22:44.112
Hold on. Why did NJ do this?

22:44.196 --> 22:47.491
Beats me. She wanted to be interviewed
as Ung's friend apparently.

22:47.574 --> 22:48.825
His friend?

22:50.160 --> 22:52.496
[Ji-ung] He's suddenly
made a new friend, that guy.

22:56.500 --> 22:58.293
Let's eat. Snap out of it.

22:58.960 --> 23:01.213
We could've had
something fancier if you wanted.

23:01.296 --> 23:03.465
It's my treat as a way of thanking you.

23:03.548 --> 23:05.258
Well, I like this place.

23:05.342 --> 23:07.219
It's where I come to
whenever I have some free time.

23:08.136 --> 23:10.430
This must be
a famous restaurant or something.

23:10.514 --> 23:12.474
- I have a great view from here.
- Of what?

23:12.557 --> 23:14.601
Of my building. Right over there.

23:17.938 --> 23:19.106
[Ung] Wow.

23:19.981 --> 23:22.901
- How much is that place?
- You mean back then or right now?

23:22.984 --> 23:24.861
How does it feel
to own a building like that?

23:25.779 --> 23:27.239
Do you mean back then or right now?

23:28.532 --> 23:31.076
Oh, you sounded
all cool and awesome just now.

23:31.159 --> 23:32.702
[chuckles]
Yeah, I know.

23:33.328 --> 23:35.288
How does it feel to finally
see the building,

23:35.372 --> 23:36.832
the one I asked you to draw?

23:36.915 --> 23:39.417
Right. You see…

23:41.128 --> 23:43.964
I just think that
it's not the best idea to draw it for you.

23:44.047 --> 23:47.259
I'm afraid it'll kinda
taint your reputation and also--

23:47.342 --> 23:48.635
And also?

23:49.553 --> 23:53.306
I'm not really motivated to draw it,
to be honest with you.

23:53.390 --> 23:55.016
[chuckles]

23:55.559 --> 23:59.437
Oh, God. For real?
Even my buildings get rejected by you.

23:59.521 --> 24:00.522
[chuckles]

24:00.605 --> 24:02.732
That really hurt my feelings.

24:02.816 --> 24:04.526
That wasn't my intention, sorry.

24:04.609 --> 24:07.320
[chuckles]
I'm just messing with you. I understand.

24:07.404 --> 24:09.865
Then don't we just
forget about that favor.

24:12.993 --> 24:15.245
[woman 1] I told you.
NJ comes here all the time.

24:15.328 --> 24:16.746
You were right.

24:17.330 --> 24:18.665
[woman 2] Hey, who's that guy
she's eating with?

24:19.249 --> 24:20.333
[woman 1] Probably her manager.

24:20.417 --> 24:23.712
You know, she's not as pretty
as I thought she'd be. Way too skinny.

24:24.713 --> 24:25.881
[woman 2] I agree.

24:25.964 --> 24:28.216
I think she got plastic surgery recently.

24:28.800 --> 24:29.926
- You see it, don't you?
- For sure.

24:30.010 --> 24:31.553
[woman 1] Let's take a photo. Quick.

24:31.636 --> 24:34.723
Let me. I have a better angle
from where I'm sitting.

24:37.726 --> 24:40.437
I'm so sorry, no photos, please.

24:41.146 --> 24:44.065
I was… we weren't taking a photo of you.

24:44.149 --> 24:46.151
We were just trying to take a selfie.

24:46.234 --> 24:47.569
[both chuckle]

24:50.572 --> 24:54.034
Probably happens way too often.
It seemed like it.

24:54.117 --> 24:57.621
Actually, it never gets old.
But I pretend like it does.

24:59.164 --> 25:02.250
Soon, they'll post it online
and leave a bunch of unpleasant comments.

25:03.335 --> 25:05.545
"I saw NJ today,
and she wasn't as pretty as I thought."

25:06.129 --> 25:09.132
"Also she didn't let me take a photo."
"Got a nasty temper too."

25:10.675 --> 25:12.469
All coming from complete strangers,

25:12.969 --> 25:14.804
but for some reason,
they think they know me

25:14.888 --> 25:16.264
and have the right to judge me.

25:18.808 --> 25:20.018
Isn't that funny?

25:21.728 --> 25:24.231
Jeez, I should've checked their phone
if they took a picture.

25:24.314 --> 25:25.899
That was way too rude.

25:25.982 --> 25:29.236
Never got why people refuse
to just understand.

25:29.319 --> 25:31.446
And are so quick to judge,
like you're nothing.

25:33.490 --> 25:34.366
[soft sigh]

25:34.449 --> 25:36.451
[light music playing]

25:38.995 --> 25:41.456
Well, don't expect them to understand.

25:44.376 --> 25:46.586
Besides, you don't even need
their understanding.

25:47.128 --> 25:50.006
Who cares? Let them do what they want,

25:50.090 --> 25:52.175
believe whatever they wanna believe.

25:52.884 --> 25:55.178
[Ung] What matters is
you understand yourself.

25:56.304 --> 25:57.722
And even that's hard.

25:59.224 --> 26:00.517
[chuckles softly]

26:02.978 --> 26:05.188
Do you wanna know one of your main charms?

26:05.272 --> 26:06.564
Oh, we're back there, huh?

26:06.648 --> 26:09.818
You're easy-going, carefree,
self-aware and not to mention, funny,

26:09.901 --> 26:12.988
so I can go on and on
about the most ridiculous things.

26:13.071 --> 26:15.407
- Is that a compliment?
- [NJ] But also,

26:15.490 --> 26:18.910
you have this serious and sincere side
to you that feels so reassuring.

26:19.411 --> 26:22.122
You tell me what I need to hear
without even trying.

26:23.665 --> 26:26.459
You're quite charming.
And that's on both sides.

26:26.543 --> 26:27.585
[chuckles]

26:28.628 --> 26:31.172
I wasn't confessing my love.
What are you all shy for?

26:32.090 --> 26:34.759
It's just, well, I've never
been good with compliments.

26:34.843 --> 26:37.929
[chuckles]
Look at that. You're also adorable.

26:38.847 --> 26:40.932
[NJ] Come on, what do you think
we should we do next?

26:41.016 --> 26:43.810
I haven't had a free day in ages.
What do we do first?

26:43.893 --> 26:46.563
[Ung] Hmm. Let's see…

26:47.939 --> 26:49.274
- Uh…
- [clicks]

26:49.357 --> 26:52.027
He was never the type to just
easily make friends with new people.

26:52.110 --> 26:53.236
He's not naturally sociable.

26:53.320 --> 26:55.155
Which makes him shy away
from any sort of contact.

26:55.238 --> 26:57.907
Always just interested in himself,
like some egomaniac.

26:57.991 --> 27:01.745
I mean, he's probably just interested
in her because she's a famous celebrity.

27:01.828 --> 27:05.165
And since he's become famous lately,
I guess he's enjoying all this.

27:05.248 --> 27:07.792
If you ask me, he should have never
revealed himself to the public.

27:07.876 --> 27:11.046
Why'd he do that? Deep down,
he was just looking for attention.

27:11.129 --> 27:13.673
But weren't you the one
who convinced him to do all of that?

27:14.257 --> 27:15.800
Exactly, why'd he need convincing?

27:17.260 --> 27:18.178
[sighs]

27:19.971 --> 27:21.056
What?

27:21.556 --> 27:24.184
You've been talking non-stop
about him for five blocks now.

27:25.560 --> 27:28.646
What should we get? You craving anything?

27:28.730 --> 27:31.066
That was a terrible shift.
You need to work on that a bit.

27:31.149 --> 27:32.776
How about some traditional cuisine?

27:35.320 --> 27:37.530
- Oh? How are you doing?
- [Ji-ung] Oh, hey, Dad!

27:37.614 --> 27:39.115
Hey, you guys.

27:39.199 --> 27:41.910
What's all this stuff you ordered?
It's like double the usual amount.

27:41.993 --> 27:44.037
We've been getting
a lot more customers lately.

27:44.120 --> 27:45.997
- [Ji-ung] Let me.
- It's fine.

27:46.081 --> 27:48.583
Oh, Dad, your back's gonna
give out real soon.

27:48.666 --> 27:50.835
[chuckles]
My back's just fine, don't you worry.

27:50.919 --> 27:52.587
Where's Ung been lately?
What's he been up to?

27:52.670 --> 27:54.589
That little rascal hasn't been picking up,
and I'm getting annoyed.

27:54.672 --> 27:56.800
Do you want me to tell him
to come over right now?

27:56.883 --> 27:58.343
- It's fine.
- [Yeok-ok] Yeon-su, you're here.

27:58.426 --> 27:59.761
Oh, hello there.

27:59.844 --> 28:01.930
I can't believe
you called Ji-ung to help us.

28:02.013 --> 28:04.057
What? Did I call you guys?
Tell this woman I didn't do it.

28:04.140 --> 28:05.725
We just stopped by for a little.
It won't take long.

28:05.809 --> 28:08.395
Oh, Ji-ung,
you're such a wonderful person.

28:08.478 --> 28:10.313
- [Yeon-ok] Thank you very much.
- You're welcome.

28:10.397 --> 28:11.815
- [Ho] No.
- It's okay, Yeon-su.

28:11.898 --> 28:14.275
They're really heavy. Don't.
Just stop. Have you eaten?

28:14.359 --> 28:16.069
Not yet. We were actually
just about to eat.

28:16.152 --> 28:18.196
- What a coincidence, eat here.
- [both chuckle]

28:18.279 --> 28:21.699
Oh, my goodness. Aren't you Ji-ung's mom?

28:21.783 --> 28:24.285
[Yeon-ok] Oh, I haven't seen you
in such a long time.

28:24.369 --> 28:26.329
[Ho] My goodness. How have you been?

28:26.413 --> 28:28.206
I hadn't seen you in ages,
so I was starting to get worried.

28:28.289 --> 28:30.583
- Have you been doing well?
- You're looking good.

28:30.667 --> 28:32.544
[Yeon-ok] Oh, you must have
been grocery shopping.

28:32.627 --> 28:34.963
- [Ho] Come inside if you haven't eaten.
- [Yeon-ok] Come inside.

28:35.046 --> 28:36.589
- Yeon-su.
- Yeah?

28:36.673 --> 28:39.050
I'm sorry, but I don't think
I can eat with you.

28:39.134 --> 28:40.802
You should stay with them and eat here.

28:42.220 --> 28:44.597
- So how have you been?
- [Ho] Yeah, what have you been up to?

28:45.098 --> 28:48.309
- Oh. Ji-ung, aren't you going to eat?
- No.

28:48.393 --> 28:49.436
[Yeon-ok] All right.

28:49.519 --> 28:50.520
Goodbye.

28:50.603 --> 28:52.188
- Goodbye.
- [Yeon-ok] Take care.

28:52.272 --> 28:54.441
- [Ho] He should have just eaten here.
- [Yeon-ok] See you.

29:00.572 --> 29:01.990
Something you need to say?

29:04.951 --> 29:06.786
You should at least sleep at home.

29:06.870 --> 29:08.872
That way you're comfortable.

29:11.499 --> 29:13.418
Or if you want, I can leave.

29:14.002 --> 29:15.712
Either way, you're gonna leave anyway.

29:18.882 --> 29:19.924
[Ji-ung sighs]

29:20.884 --> 29:22.427
[soft music]

29:22.510 --> 29:23.845
Can you do me a favor?

29:25.805 --> 29:28.391
I really care about
all those people back there,

29:29.934 --> 29:32.353
so I don't want them
to ever see this side of me.

29:35.899 --> 29:37.192
Be your usual self.

29:39.110 --> 29:40.695
Ignore them and be on your way.

29:45.992 --> 29:48.161
[soft music continues]

29:50.622 --> 29:52.582
[footsteps receding]

29:54.375 --> 29:56.127
[whooshing]

29:58.880 --> 30:01.466
Again, I'm seeing
a totally new side of you.

30:02.300 --> 30:04.427
- Huh?
- You didn't strike me as the type of guy

30:04.511 --> 30:06.638
who owned a car
or even knew how to drive one.

30:06.721 --> 30:10.308
- Hmm. I like this.
- What? Oh, I thought you meant…

30:10.391 --> 30:11.851
Well, be more specific, Ung.

30:13.019 --> 30:14.187
[NJ huffs]

30:14.270 --> 30:17.440
Oh! Sorry. I didn't mean like…

30:17.524 --> 30:20.360
this, as in us, I meant driving.
[chuckles awkwardly]

30:20.443 --> 30:22.570
It's just that Eun-ho usually drives,

30:22.654 --> 30:26.825
and I rarely have to travel far anyway.
I'm not outdoorsy.

30:27.450 --> 30:30.161
I really wanted us to have a blast today.

30:30.245 --> 30:32.705
I'm sorry we kept
running away from everyone.

30:32.789 --> 30:35.250
It's fascinating, everyone recognizes you.

30:35.834 --> 30:37.919
So what do you like to do
when you're all by yourself?

30:38.002 --> 30:40.630
Hmm… When I'm by myself?

30:40.713 --> 30:43.341
Well, I enjoy just doing nothing.

30:43.424 --> 30:44.884
Then what did you do yesterday?

30:46.594 --> 30:47.554
Uh…

30:48.763 --> 30:49.764
I was…

30:53.810 --> 30:55.311
[breathes in deeply]

30:55.395 --> 30:57.897
I really don't want to be
this kind of girl,

30:58.898 --> 31:00.817
but can I ask you something personal?

31:03.152 --> 31:04.946
What's your relationship with Ms. Kook?

31:07.699 --> 31:08.533
Uh…

31:08.616 --> 31:11.202
Like back then or right now?

31:12.412 --> 31:13.496
Either.

31:13.580 --> 31:14.414
[soft chuckle]

31:15.456 --> 31:16.499
Well, back then…

31:17.792 --> 31:19.294
I really liked her.

31:20.545 --> 31:23.298
I didn't know I could be
that madly in love.

31:23.381 --> 31:25.383
[light music]

31:26.050 --> 31:27.886
Mm… But now…

31:30.680 --> 31:32.056
well, we're just friends.

31:33.016 --> 31:36.269
Tell me, how does it feel
to love someone as much as you loved her?

31:37.061 --> 31:38.146
I'm very curious.

31:38.646 --> 31:41.900
Like how could you still talk about her
like that without breaking down

31:41.983 --> 31:43.484
even though you two are over?

31:45.403 --> 31:47.405
Actually, no, don't.

31:47.488 --> 31:49.782
Forget about that question.
I'm not curious anymore.

31:50.366 --> 31:51.576
[chuckles]

31:52.577 --> 31:54.537
Oh, sorry,
I think we're getting close now.

31:54.621 --> 31:56.956
Yeah, we are. Turn left over there.

32:01.252 --> 32:03.755
[light music]

32:06.215 --> 32:07.592
[music stops]

32:12.180 --> 32:13.890
Thank you very much for dropping me off.

32:14.557 --> 32:16.184
- You take care.
- I will.

32:16.267 --> 32:17.769
Wait.

32:17.852 --> 32:21.564
You shouldn't try to put
too much meaning into what happened today.

32:22.190 --> 32:23.274
Just get some rest.

32:26.778 --> 32:27.904
Hold on a sec.

32:28.571 --> 32:32.200
I just thought it'd be a shame
to end my super rare free day like this.

32:32.283 --> 32:35.328
- But there's nowhere we can even--
- Do you wanna come up?

32:46.172 --> 32:48.257
[cheeky music]

32:55.348 --> 32:57.976
[Yeon-su] I'm not saying this
because it's bothering me or anything.

32:58.601 --> 33:00.812
I'm just curious, which is a normal thing.

33:00.895 --> 33:03.064
Just what are those two up to?

33:03.648 --> 33:04.565
[scoffs]

33:04.649 --> 33:06.192
As if they're actually friends.

33:06.275 --> 33:08.820
Were they even schoolmates,
colleagues or neighbors at least.

33:08.903 --> 33:10.154
How can they be friends

33:10.238 --> 33:12.407
when they don't even have
any shared memories together?

33:12.490 --> 33:13.908
[annoyed sigh]

33:15.785 --> 33:17.495
They can't still be together, right?

33:18.246 --> 33:20.164
Because if he had lunch outside then,

33:20.248 --> 33:22.583
wouldn't it make sense
to just have dinner at home?

33:25.461 --> 33:27.255
[yelps]
God, that's cold!

33:27.338 --> 33:29.382
- Oh.
- What are you trying to do to me?

33:29.465 --> 33:31.801
- Oh, my goodness.
- Oh, do you have a blindfold on?

33:31.884 --> 33:33.761
Are you trying to do it on purpose?

33:33.845 --> 33:35.972
It's okay.
It wasn't that much, just relax.

33:36.055 --> 33:39.684
What do you mean? It's all over there.
I feel like I'm being drenched here.

33:39.767 --> 33:40.643
You're not.

33:40.727 --> 33:42.645
Will you please just concentrate
some more?

33:42.729 --> 33:45.648
It's 'cause you were dozing off, grandma.
Stop deflecting, it's bad.

33:45.732 --> 33:47.358
Lift up your head a bit more. Hmm?

33:48.484 --> 33:50.737
[groans]

33:51.654 --> 33:53.865
Oh, my God, what the hell just happened?

33:54.866 --> 33:56.242
Listen, NJ.

33:57.410 --> 33:59.120
I think I should just go home now.

34:00.913 --> 34:01.831
Okay.

34:01.914 --> 34:04.333
Did you really have to get out of the car
just so you could reject me?

34:04.917 --> 34:06.961
Well, I had to,
since you were asking so politely.

34:07.045 --> 34:08.629
Hold on a sec. You got it all wrong.

34:08.713 --> 34:11.758
Don't overthink this. It was just
a thought that crossed my mind.

34:11.841 --> 34:14.594
You took it way too seriously
by overreacting,

34:14.677 --> 34:16.137
and now I feel embarrassed.

34:16.220 --> 34:17.972
Okay, I'm sorry.

34:18.056 --> 34:20.641
I said that wasn't necessary.
You're still overreacting.

34:20.725 --> 34:22.518
You know how ridiculous
you're being right now?

34:22.602 --> 34:24.562
I wasn't asking you
to date me or anything.

34:24.645 --> 34:26.898
I didn't wanna say goodbye yet,
so I thought we could go up

34:26.981 --> 34:29.025
and chat in a nice private place.

34:29.108 --> 34:30.443
This is how I am.

34:30.526 --> 34:32.361
It takes time to warm up to someone.

34:32.445 --> 34:33.905
[groans]
I mean,

34:33.988 --> 34:36.866
for God's sake, it's already been a month.
How much slower do we need to go?

34:37.867 --> 34:40.328
He's going to stay
as my crush forever at this rate.

34:40.828 --> 34:42.288
[annoyed sigh]

34:42.997 --> 34:45.208
[cheeky music]

34:46.375 --> 34:47.543
Well…

34:48.920 --> 34:52.131
Having a crush
isn't such a bad thing actually.

34:54.175 --> 34:57.386
I can wait. I can wait.

34:58.012 --> 34:58.930
#NJ
1.81 MILLION POSTS

34:59.013 --> 35:01.390
APDLW_J
548 LIKES

35:01.474 --> 35:03.309
[woman 2] I saw the famous NJ today.

35:03.392 --> 35:05.520
I asked her for a photo,
and then she downright ignored me.

35:05.603 --> 35:06.896
She does have an awful temper.

35:06.979 --> 35:09.941
And is she really that pretty?
Oh, I beg to differ.

35:10.024 --> 35:11.484
[trol 1] NJ has an awful personality.

35:11.567 --> 35:13.361
[trol 2] How hard is it to agree?

35:13.444 --> 35:14.612
[troles all commenting]

35:14.695 --> 35:16.197
[trol 3] It's your job
to have your photo taken.

35:16.280 --> 35:17.281
[music fades]

35:21.953 --> 35:24.038
I… I left something at your place.

35:24.122 --> 35:26.124
I need to go and get it right now,
if that's okay.

35:27.750 --> 35:30.253
It's something I need.
It's super precious to me.

35:30.336 --> 35:31.587
[chuckles]

35:33.923 --> 35:35.258
[chuckles joyously]

35:36.676 --> 35:38.803
[quirky music]

35:44.809 --> 35:46.269
[breathes in sharply]

35:47.770 --> 35:49.397
Technically as a friend,

35:49.480 --> 35:52.108
it wouldn't be too weird
if I asked him what he's up to.

35:52.191 --> 35:54.735
[breathes deeply]

35:55.444 --> 35:58.656
Don't hide it. That's what
having a secret crush feels like.

36:00.575 --> 36:01.993
That's not true.

36:02.076 --> 36:03.494
Are you almost done?

36:06.956 --> 36:09.041
[quirky music continues]

36:11.169 --> 36:14.881
[Yeon-su] This isn't like…
I mean, I don't have a crush on him.

36:16.549 --> 36:18.301
Hmm? What is this?

36:18.926 --> 36:22.013
What the… What are you…
What is all this? Huh?

36:23.264 --> 36:25.308
It looks like green sausages in there.

36:25.391 --> 36:27.977
Who puts zucchini this big
into their soup, hm?

36:28.686 --> 36:30.313
What in the world is the matter with you?

36:31.189 --> 36:34.275
I bet this… What have you done?
[sighs]

36:35.902 --> 36:36.736
[gasps softly]

36:40.072 --> 36:42.158
[quirky music]

36:50.082 --> 36:51.083
[gate clanks]

36:53.586 --> 36:54.545
[gate closes]

36:58.299 --> 37:02.053
["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim playing]

37:09.227 --> 37:10.478
[Yeon-su] This is really bad.

37:13.898 --> 37:15.233
I guess I was wrong.

37:19.237 --> 37:21.197
I still have feelings for him.

37:24.033 --> 37:26.535
["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim continues]

37:33.376 --> 37:34.585
This yours?

37:36.337 --> 37:38.047
Yeah, it is.

37:40.549 --> 37:43.052
Was this
that super precious pouch of yours?

37:44.470 --> 37:46.013
Is this why you came here?

37:48.140 --> 37:51.519
Yeah, well, you said
it was really precious to you.

37:54.313 --> 37:55.648
And is that all?

37:58.317 --> 37:59.777
[Yeon-su] I can't deny it.

38:03.572 --> 38:04.949
I don't think that…

38:07.243 --> 38:10.204
I ever forgot about him,
even for a second.

38:21.257 --> 38:22.591
You know what?

38:26.887 --> 38:28.097
I…

38:29.056 --> 38:30.391
I think that…

38:30.474 --> 38:32.226
[Ja-gyeong] Who is that out there?

38:33.602 --> 38:34.895
[music fades]

38:39.275 --> 38:40.276
[slurps]

39:00.588 --> 39:02.840
You know that I haven't seen you in years.

39:03.716 --> 39:05.593
So why did you suddenly show up?

39:06.218 --> 39:07.345
Grandma.

39:07.928 --> 39:09.805
You're the one who invited him inside.

39:09.889 --> 39:13.642
Because he said he hadn't eaten yet.
Of course I should feed him.

39:14.852 --> 39:17.188
What are you doing? Eat up. Go.

39:20.733 --> 39:23.611
All right. Be straight.
Are you two dating again?

39:25.363 --> 39:29.158
Grandma, what?
Just let him eat in peace, will you?

39:29.241 --> 39:31.577
Also, it's not like that.
We're just friends.

39:31.660 --> 39:33.913
"We're just friends", my foot.

39:33.996 --> 39:35.748
Were you that desperate to have a friend?

39:38.417 --> 39:40.252
What's wrong with you? Eat up.

39:40.336 --> 39:41.379
Oh. Yeah.

39:41.462 --> 39:43.881
Look at him nibbling on like a rat.

39:43.964 --> 39:46.634
- Is it bad?
- Oh, it's delicious.

39:46.717 --> 39:49.595
Hey. Slow it down. You don't wanna choke.

39:49.678 --> 39:53.307
You gotta be rock bottom desperate
to be friends with your ex.

39:54.183 --> 39:56.394
That other boy is
a whole lot better. Ji-ung.

39:57.353 --> 40:01.607
He's got good manners, he's well-behaved,
looks respectable and cute too.

40:02.441 --> 40:06.070
On the other hand, look at this guy.
He's a useless sack of potatoes.

40:07.655 --> 40:09.031
Hey, I'm sorry.

40:09.115 --> 40:12.493
She hasn't changed. You know
she likes to badmouth people openly.

40:12.576 --> 40:13.411
[chuckles softly]

40:14.995 --> 40:17.623
Are you even able to eat well, at least?

40:17.706 --> 40:20.126
Looks like you got a lot skinnier now.

40:21.001 --> 40:25.506
So tell me. Do you even have
a decent job to support yourself?

40:25.589 --> 40:26.549
Hmm…

40:27.174 --> 40:28.467
[clears throat]

40:28.551 --> 40:30.970
- I asked you a question, answer!
- [coughs]

40:31.053 --> 40:34.098
Still just as reserved and shy
as if he never grew a spine.

40:34.181 --> 40:37.435
Grandma, quit it. Stop scolding him.
He's trying to eat, like you asked him.

40:37.518 --> 40:40.604
What's wrong? Why are you being
so cold towards him all of a sudden?

40:40.688 --> 40:43.065
You want me to be kind
to someone who made you cry?

40:44.150 --> 40:45.860
I'd love to beat his ass up.

40:49.196 --> 40:51.323
[gentle vulnerable music]

41:00.082 --> 41:01.041
[Ung sighs]

41:03.502 --> 41:06.380
Hey. You don't have to do this. Just go.

41:07.590 --> 41:10.176
I know you're uncomfortable.
You should go.

41:10.259 --> 41:12.595
I wanna apologize for her behavior.

41:13.345 --> 41:15.055
I should still eat anyway.

41:22.897 --> 41:24.023
[sighs]

41:24.106 --> 41:26.108
[gentle music]

41:31.155 --> 41:34.408
You're just eating plain rice.
Don't skip the side dishes.

41:34.492 --> 41:35.743
Thank you.

41:35.826 --> 41:37.912
[gentle music continues]

41:47.505 --> 41:49.381
[sighs in relief]

41:49.465 --> 41:51.383
God, look at this belly.

41:51.467 --> 41:52.718
You think it's a boy or a girl?

41:53.302 --> 41:56.013
You know, you shouldn't have overeaten.
Why did you have two extra bowls?

41:56.096 --> 41:58.015
She gave me more soup if I had rice left

41:58.098 --> 42:00.267
and gave me more rice if I had soup left.
I had no choice.

42:01.060 --> 42:02.811
I haven't eaten this much in a while.

42:02.895 --> 42:04.021
[chuckles]

42:04.104 --> 42:06.190
She's still the same, your grandma.

42:06.857 --> 42:08.692
And still scary as ever.

42:08.776 --> 42:10.319
[both chuckling]

42:19.203 --> 42:20.287
Later.

42:21.580 --> 42:22.623
Hmm.

42:26.961 --> 42:27.920
Hey, Ung.

42:30.589 --> 42:31.590
I…

42:33.634 --> 42:34.635
Thank you.

42:36.428 --> 42:37.721
For what?

42:40.641 --> 42:41.809
Uh…

42:44.061 --> 42:46.689
For my pouch, thanks for bringing it back.

42:49.108 --> 42:50.025
See that?

42:51.485 --> 42:53.862
I guess we can really
be friends after all, right?

42:57.408 --> 42:59.535
[gentle music]

43:06.667 --> 43:08.711
[gentle music continues]

43:16.719 --> 43:18.554
Grandma, just let me do it.

43:19.597 --> 43:20.514
Okay.

43:22.474 --> 43:24.018
Did he leave yet?

43:24.602 --> 43:25.519
[Yeon-su] Yes.

43:27.396 --> 43:29.898
- Hmm. Could have stayed longer.
- [water trickling]

43:29.982 --> 43:31.025
Why didn't he?

43:31.108 --> 43:34.403
You really expected him to stay
after giving him an earful?

43:34.987 --> 43:37.281
Besides, I thought you wanted him gone.

43:37.364 --> 43:39.366
Now, why would you assume that?

43:40.451 --> 43:42.995
But it is true that
he gave you a hard time.

43:45.331 --> 43:47.041
So when did you see me cry?

43:47.124 --> 43:50.544
Oh, please, you were secretly crying
for days on end. I was so worried.

43:50.628 --> 43:52.338
You expected me not to notice that?

43:53.589 --> 43:56.050
Just thinking about it
makes my blood boil.

43:56.133 --> 43:58.135
That good for nothing scumbag.

43:58.218 --> 44:00.846
In fact, I should have been
a whole lot harsher than that.

44:02.806 --> 44:04.350
[water running]

44:17.821 --> 44:20.616
["The Giving Tree"
by Lee Seung Yoon playing]

44:31.377 --> 44:33.087
I was the one who broke up with him.

44:35.964 --> 44:37.966
[Yeon-su] I pretty much abandoned him.

44:40.219 --> 44:41.220
Hmm?

44:42.596 --> 44:43.722
[sobs]

44:45.641 --> 44:47.267
It was basically my fault.

44:49.478 --> 44:50.854
I was being selfish.

44:52.690 --> 44:54.274
But, Yeon-su…

44:55.943 --> 44:57.194
And grandma…

44:59.905 --> 45:02.157
I still have feelings for Choi Ung.

45:05.411 --> 45:06.870
Despite I abandoning him…

45:07.704 --> 45:08.914
and letting him go,

45:10.499 --> 45:11.583
I still…

45:12.835 --> 45:14.878
He never left my heart at all.

45:18.006 --> 45:19.133
[Yeon-su] So that's why…

45:20.217 --> 45:22.386
you ought to be shouting at me instead.

45:24.805 --> 45:26.974
Tell me that I was being stupid and cruel.

45:28.183 --> 45:29.518
Because I deserve it.

45:31.061 --> 45:34.064
Ask me why I would do something
that I'd regret later on.

45:36.066 --> 45:37.151
So, please…

45:38.318 --> 45:39.361
Just say something.

45:40.904 --> 45:42.030
Yeon-su…

45:44.241 --> 45:46.160
What should I do, grandma?

45:46.243 --> 45:48.412
["The Giving Tree"
by Lee Seung Yoon continues]

45:50.622 --> 45:52.958
'Cause I can't handle being just friends.

45:54.668 --> 45:55.544
I can't.

45:58.088 --> 46:00.799
But I guess for him it's a lot easier.
[sad chuckle]

46:02.843 --> 46:05.304
I have no idea what I should do.
[sniffles]

46:06.889 --> 46:08.932
[Yeon-su sniffles softly]

46:17.191 --> 46:18.859
Oh, my poor girl.

46:25.949 --> 46:27.367
[sniffles]

46:32.706 --> 46:34.208
[Yeon-su crying]

46:36.168 --> 46:38.712
["The Giving Tree" continuing]

46:59.983 --> 47:01.652
BEFORE OUR SUMMER

47:03.862 --> 47:06.365
["The Giving Tree"
by Lee Seung Yoon playing]

47:09.535 --> 47:10.619
[sighs]

47:20.963 --> 47:21.797
[music fades]

47:23.006 --> 47:25.050
[keyboard clacking]

47:25.592 --> 47:29.012
Look at Ms. Kook.
Her eyes are swollen like crazy.

47:30.097 --> 47:31.348
Speaking from experience,

47:31.431 --> 47:34.309
she probably cried all night
for at least five hours minimum.

47:35.102 --> 47:36.270
[I-hun yawns]

47:36.353 --> 47:39.314
I'm so exhausted. I really am. Going home.

47:39.898 --> 47:42.442
Ugh, it's such a lazy afternoon,
what's going on?

47:42.526 --> 47:45.571
We should probably have some coffee
to help us stay awake, right? You in?

47:45.654 --> 47:46.905
- Coffee sounds great.
- You all in?

47:46.989 --> 47:48.949
How about we play Ghost Leg
to spice it up?

47:49.032 --> 47:50.409
- Yeah? Okay?
- Uh-huh.

47:50.492 --> 47:53.245
Ji-un, let's go. Get everything ready.
Okay. Go.

47:53.328 --> 47:54.788
[keyboard clacking]

47:55.372 --> 47:56.206
Ms. Kook.

47:57.666 --> 47:59.334
[laughs]

48:01.086 --> 48:02.838
Wow, have you guys seen her eyes?
[laughs]

48:02.921 --> 48:04.548
What's wrong?
[chuckles]

48:04.631 --> 48:07.467
Did you notice
what her eyes look like today? Wow.

48:08.176 --> 48:09.011
Wow.

48:09.678 --> 48:11.388
You look a little different than usual.

48:12.723 --> 48:15.017
A carp. She looks like a carp fish.
[laughs loudly]

48:15.767 --> 48:17.811
What's the matter?
Did you cry last night or something?

48:17.894 --> 48:20.188
'Cause if that's not it,
then how could you look like this?

48:20.272 --> 48:22.024
No, I didn't cry.

48:23.525 --> 48:25.068
I got a sty on my eye.

48:26.153 --> 48:28.196
- Huh?
- I said that it's…

48:29.281 --> 48:31.491
a sty, sir.

48:32.576 --> 48:33.660
[gulps]

48:36.788 --> 48:38.498
- It's a sty, guys.
- [all laughing awkwardly]

48:38.582 --> 48:40.751
- It's a sty.
- I knew it.

48:40.834 --> 48:42.711
It's a sty. I told you
from the beginning, right?

48:43.337 --> 48:44.504
Anyway, since she has a sty,

48:44.588 --> 48:46.840
I say we all focus
and do a good job. Let's go.

48:46.923 --> 48:48.592
- All right. Yes, sir.
- Okay, good.

48:48.675 --> 48:49.968
- The Ghost Leg?
- Pass.

48:50.052 --> 48:51.678
Stick with what you're doing.

48:55.932 --> 48:58.352
[awkward music]

49:00.771 --> 49:01.647
[mirror clicks]

49:04.149 --> 49:05.317
[sighs]

49:07.444 --> 49:08.487
[sighs deeply]

49:11.156 --> 49:13.367
[Ho] Well, well, what brings you here?

49:13.450 --> 49:16.036
What's the matter?
Couldn't handle all the adoring fans?

49:16.828 --> 49:19.206
No reason. It just felt weird
to be all alone at home.

49:19.289 --> 49:21.750
You've always been alone
in that big old house.

49:21.833 --> 49:23.919
So why did you even move out
in the first place?

49:24.002 --> 49:25.337
I told you to just move back in.

49:25.420 --> 49:29.049
Jeez. No matter how hard you try,
it won't work. I won't be swayed.

49:29.132 --> 49:30.050
[scoffs]

49:30.133 --> 49:31.510
[Yeon-ok] Then what if it's me?

49:32.094 --> 49:33.345
Then I could be swayed a bit.

49:33.428 --> 49:34.554
[chuckles happily]

49:34.638 --> 49:36.932
Wow, you treacherous little punk.

49:37.015 --> 49:39.059
You don't deserve to sit on my bench.
So move your butt.

49:39.142 --> 49:40.769
No, you move your butt.

49:40.852 --> 49:43.271
- Suit yourself, you little traitor.
- [chuckling]

49:44.106 --> 49:45.107
- Hey, Ung.
- Hmm?

49:45.190 --> 49:48.110
Call Ji-ung right now and ask him
if he plans to have dinner somewhere.

49:48.193 --> 49:50.570
If not, tell him to come here instead.
I made lots of food.

49:51.154 --> 49:53.240
Well, I spoke to him earlier,
he said he was gonna be working late.

49:53.323 --> 49:56.118
You know he's always pretending
to be busy and stuff. It's annoying.

49:56.201 --> 49:57.994
[Yeon-ok] Really?
Oh, that's not good at all.

49:58.078 --> 50:00.080
That boy needs to have
at least a proper meal today.

50:00.163 --> 50:03.333
Oh, you know what? I'll just pick
one of each and pack his dinner.

50:03.417 --> 50:05.585
- Can you drop it off later to him?
- [groans]

50:05.669 --> 50:08.213
Just call a delivery service.
I'll even pay for it.

50:08.296 --> 50:11.258
Not a chance. Don't be ridiculous.
Not like you're doing anything anyway.

50:11.341 --> 50:13.301
[whines]
I can't be bothered.

50:13.385 --> 50:15.053
How about you tell him
to come late and eat?

50:15.137 --> 50:17.556
No, not today. Hurry up and get ready.

50:18.974 --> 50:20.142
Man.

50:22.018 --> 50:23.395
[clicks tongue, whining groan]

50:24.521 --> 50:25.689
[phone buzzing]

50:30.652 --> 50:32.487
[Ji-ung's mother]
You should sleep at home tonight.

50:33.071 --> 50:34.531
Don't worry, I'm not there anymore.

50:40.912 --> 50:42.748
Ji-ung, are you going to the editing room?

50:45.500 --> 50:46.334
Ji-ung.

50:48.044 --> 50:49.921
- Huh?
- Are you editing right now?

50:51.506 --> 50:52.549
Oh. Yeah.

50:53.550 --> 50:56.094
Oh. Yeah, right. Can you leave this there?
I need to go now.

50:56.178 --> 50:58.472
I'm gonna go home and wash up,
and change clothes.

50:58.555 --> 51:00.307
Ji-ung, did you
spend the night here again?

51:00.390 --> 51:01.516
Yeah.
[sighs]

51:02.726 --> 51:04.728
Please do that for me. I'll be back.

51:15.447 --> 51:17.532
[soft music]

51:35.050 --> 51:36.009
[door closes]

51:47.103 --> 51:49.105
[soft music continues]

52:01.701 --> 52:02.786
[sighs]

52:05.413 --> 52:06.790
[chuckles sadly]

52:11.837 --> 52:13.839
[soft sob]

52:17.759 --> 52:20.679
[sobbing]

52:29.771 --> 52:31.106
Look who's here!

52:31.189 --> 52:33.900
- Ung!
- Oh, Mr. Park.

52:33.984 --> 52:36.236
[Dong-il] Wow. Look at you, huh?

52:36.319 --> 52:38.989
You haven't changed one bit,
you little rascal!

52:39.072 --> 52:41.825
I saw the footage of you so far,
and you really hadn't changed at all.

52:41.908 --> 52:44.286
- You still look like a flipping student.
- [gasps]

52:44.369 --> 52:46.746
Same with you. You still look like
you're in your thirties.

52:47.372 --> 52:48.582
I am in my thirties.

52:50.584 --> 52:52.377
Exactly. You look like it.

52:52.460 --> 52:53.712
Huh.

52:53.795 --> 52:55.672
[both chuckling]

52:55.755 --> 52:57.507
What are you doing here?
Are you visiting Ji-ung?

52:57.591 --> 52:59.009
Oh, do you know where he is?

52:59.092 --> 53:01.887
Ah, him and Chae-ran are practically
living in the editing room these days.

53:02.470 --> 53:03.930
- Follow me. I'll take you there.
- Oh. Okay.

53:04.014 --> 53:07.017
Wow, dude. Made a name for yourself, huh?

53:07.100 --> 53:09.686
You know, even though you had
the lowest grades in school,

53:09.769 --> 53:11.730
I saw your potential,
your drawings said it all.

53:11.813 --> 53:13.106
I just knew you'd make it.

53:13.189 --> 53:16.318
- My God. How are your parents doing?
- [Ung] They're well.

53:16.818 --> 53:19.237
- Chae-ran! Where'd Ji-ung go?
- [gasps]

53:19.321 --> 53:22.824
Uh, he just left so he can stop
by his house to change and stuff.

53:22.908 --> 53:24.576
Oh, is that so. Is he coming back?

53:25.160 --> 53:27.746
Uh, he said it won't take long.
Just a quick house run.

53:27.829 --> 53:30.081
- [Chae-ran] He'll be back soon.
- Oh, okay.

53:30.165 --> 53:33.293
Hey, Ung, you just wait here.
Ji-ung will be back soon.

53:33.376 --> 53:34.377
- Okay.
- Good.

53:34.461 --> 53:36.296
Chae-ran, out. Come out. Come here.

53:36.379 --> 53:37.839
- I have something to tell you. Quick.
- Okay.

53:42.761 --> 53:44.471
Oh, boy.
[sighs]

53:47.057 --> 53:48.266
Huh?

53:48.975 --> 53:49.893
[groans]

53:52.187 --> 53:53.688
[chuckles softly]

53:55.023 --> 53:56.775
What do I need to press here?

54:01.738 --> 54:02.989
[chuckles]

54:05.075 --> 54:06.534
[sighs]

54:09.204 --> 54:12.791
[sighs]
Exactly how slow do I need to be for you?

54:12.874 --> 54:14.334
MR. CHOI UNG

54:15.251 --> 54:17.128
[groans]
Should I call or not?

54:22.384 --> 54:23.593
[phone buzzing]

54:24.552 --> 54:25.971
Good evening.

54:27.305 --> 54:28.348
[Chi-seong] Excuse me?

54:30.934 --> 54:32.227
Okay. Fine, I'll check.

54:33.186 --> 54:34.396
[dial tone]

54:36.982 --> 54:38.775
Please pick up for once.

54:41.236 --> 54:42.654
[Yeon-su sighing]

54:43.238 --> 54:45.156
I can't believe my eyes are still red.

54:46.491 --> 54:48.410
I'm never going to cry again.

54:48.493 --> 54:49.828
[phone buzzing]

54:52.205 --> 54:53.665
[buzzing continues]

54:58.086 --> 55:00.422
- What is it?
- [Sol-i] Working late?

55:01.589 --> 55:03.550
No, I clocked out.

55:03.633 --> 55:06.052
[Sol-i] Well… Are you okay?

55:06.136 --> 55:07.137
With what?

55:07.971 --> 55:09.556
[Sol-i] Haven't you seen the news yet?

55:10.974 --> 55:11.891
About what?

55:11.975 --> 55:15.270
[Sol-i] About NJ's latest dating rumor.

55:15.353 --> 55:16.563
Ji-ung?

55:16.646 --> 55:17.981
[Sol-i] The thing is…

55:18.064 --> 55:19.649
- Wait, hold on.
- [Sol-i] Choi--

55:20.442 --> 55:21.985
[Yeon-su] What brings you out here?

55:23.278 --> 55:24.738
Going home now?

55:27.032 --> 55:28.450
You must have clocked out early.

55:31.536 --> 55:33.121
Oh. Uh…

55:33.955 --> 55:37.250
Actually, I'm rushing so I should
get going now. Have a good night.

55:45.425 --> 55:48.428
Hey. Is something going on?

55:52.432 --> 55:53.349
Yeon-su.

55:55.143 --> 55:56.019
Hmm?

55:57.228 --> 55:58.438
Today is my birthday.

55:59.814 --> 56:01.816
Oh, really?

56:02.442 --> 56:03.276
Happy birthday.

56:03.359 --> 56:06.446
If I had known sooner, I would have
treated you to a fancy meal or something.

56:08.031 --> 56:10.492
My mom came by
and prepared a birthday meal for me.

56:11.910 --> 56:13.703
She's the woman I saw before, right?

56:14.829 --> 56:17.749
That was my first time seeing her.
She's a beautiful woman.

56:21.044 --> 56:22.462
She still doesn't know…

56:25.799 --> 56:28.134
She still doesn't know
that I'm allergic to peaches.

56:33.973 --> 56:35.141
One time…

56:37.727 --> 56:38.895
I almost died…

56:42.065 --> 56:44.818
and this was right in front of her
after eating a peach.

56:46.194 --> 56:48.154
But I guess she still doesn't know.

56:50.115 --> 56:52.492
Hey. Hey, Ji-ung…

56:52.575 --> 56:55.078
[somber music]

56:59.082 --> 57:01.417
Are… are you okay?

57:04.045 --> 57:05.713
Or maybe she never really cared.

57:08.174 --> 57:10.301
["Home" by Janet Suhh playing]

57:33.867 --> 57:35.994
CURRENT AFFAIRS AND CULTURE
KIM JI-UNG

57:40.999 --> 57:44.627
EPILOGUE
NOVEMBER, 2010

57:54.429 --> 57:56.055
What are you, frozen?

57:57.932 --> 58:00.059
Hey, can I sleep over at your house today?

58:01.102 --> 58:02.187
Sure, of course you can.

58:03.938 --> 58:07.108
["Home" by Janet Suhh continues]

58:16.534 --> 58:17.952
[groans]

58:20.163 --> 58:21.206
[groans]

58:23.333 --> 58:24.834
How is that even possible?

58:25.919 --> 58:27.754
[both laughing]

58:29.297 --> 58:31.299
[Ji-ung] What do you think about that?

58:31.382 --> 58:32.467
That's crazy.

58:34.302 --> 58:35.345
I know.

58:35.428 --> 58:36.387
- Sleepy?
- No.

58:38.848 --> 58:39.766
[sighs]

58:49.192 --> 58:52.362
THE PREVIOUS NIGHT

58:54.447 --> 58:55.865
Aren't you working?

58:55.949 --> 58:57.951
[Ung yawning]
Oh, my God.

58:59.035 --> 58:59.911
[groans]

59:01.579 --> 59:02.497
[groans]

59:02.580 --> 59:03.790
So tell me.

59:04.749 --> 59:05.625
What?

59:05.708 --> 59:07.752
I'm all ears, so spill it. Come on.

59:14.092 --> 59:15.552
My mom came by.

59:22.976 --> 59:24.978
She came unannounced just like before.

59:28.231 --> 59:31.818
Judging by the size of her suitcase,
I think she'll be here for about a week.

59:33.903 --> 59:35.863
She'll act as if
she'll be staying with me.

59:37.532 --> 59:39.742
And then she'll vanish once again.

59:41.160 --> 59:43.997
[sighs]
How many times has she done this?

59:44.998 --> 59:45.915
[scoffs]

59:45.999 --> 59:48.376
You know, she even
made breakfast this morning somehow.

59:48.459 --> 59:49.502
Terrible cook.

59:50.878 --> 59:53.339
["Drawer" by 10CM playing]

59:55.550 --> 01:00:02.557
HELLO, MY SOULMATE

01:00:25.413 --> 01:00:27.999
Yeah, she's pretty,
but she's not Ung's type.

01:00:28.583 --> 01:00:30.251
[Yeon-su] What's the probability
of your ex ending up

01:00:30.335 --> 01:00:33.171
in a scandal with a celebrity
in your lifetime?

01:00:33.755 --> 01:00:35.256
[Ji-ung] Someone once told me

01:00:35.340 --> 01:00:37.842
that everything I shoot
is full of emotion.

01:00:38.926 --> 01:00:42.096
Ung, about us being just friends…

01:00:42.180 --> 01:00:44.015
I don't think I can do that.

01:00:44.098 --> 01:00:45.475
[Ung] You're drunk.

01:00:45.558 --> 01:00:49.312
I don't think I can face something
that I can't handle again.

01:00:51.147 --> 01:00:52.190
Are you and Ung…

01:00:53.066 --> 01:00:54.942
What you read in the article is true.

01:00:55.026 --> 01:00:57.236
[NJ] Ung and I are dating.
